<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<aiml version="1.0.1" xmlns="http://alicebot.org/2001/AIML-1.0.1"
      xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:schemaLocation="http://alicebot.org/2001/AIML-1.0.1 http://alicebot.org/2001/AIML-1.0.1/AIML.xsd">

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- GREETINGS                                                      -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <category>
    <pattern>HI</pattern>
    <template>Hello! 👋 I am the Family Relationship Chatbot. Ask me about family relations like "who is the father of Ali" or "chacha of Laiba". How can I help you?</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HI *</pattern>
    <template>Hello there! 😊 Ask me anything about the family tree. Try: "father of ali" or "who is grandfather of zain".</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HELLO</pattern>
    <template>Hello! 👋 I am your Family Relationship Assistant. I can find relations like father, mother, uncle, chacha, dada, nana and more. What would you like to know?</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HELLO *</pattern>
    <template>Hi there! Ready to explore the family tree. Try asking: "who is the sister of ali" or "mother of zain".</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HEY</pattern>
    <template>Hey! 🤖 Welcome to the Family Chatbot. I can answer questions about any family relationship. What would you like to know?</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HEY *</pattern>
    <template>Hey! I'm here to help with family relationship queries. What would you like to find out?</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>GREETINGS</pattern>
    <template>Greetings! 🌟 I am the Family Relationship Chatbot powered by Prolog AI. Ask me about any family member and their relations!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>SALAAM</pattern>
    <template>Wa Alaikum Assalam! 🌙 Welcome! I can help you discover family relationships. Try asking: "who is chacha of laiba" or "dada of zain".</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>ASSALAM O ALAIKUM</pattern>
    <template>Wa Alaikum Assalam! 🌙 Welcome to the Family Relationship Chatbot. I support both Western and Eastern (Urdu) relation names. How can I assist you today?</template>
  </category>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- SMALL TALK                                                     -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW ARE YOU</pattern>
    <template>I am doing great, thank you for asking! 😊 I am always ready to answer your family relationship questions. What would you like to know?</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW ARE YOU *</pattern>
    <template>I am functioning perfectly! Thanks for asking. Let me help you explore the family tree today.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS YOUR NAME</pattern>
    <template>My name is FamilyBot 🤖 — your intelligent Family Relationship Assistant powered by Prolog + AIML + Python!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT IS YOUR NAME *</pattern>
    <template>I go by FamilyBot! I am an AI chatbot that reasons about family relationships using a Prolog knowledge base.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHO ARE YOU</pattern>
    <template>I am FamilyBot 🤖 — an intelligent chatbot that uses Prolog symbolic reasoning to answer questions about family relationships. I support relations like father, mother, uncle, aunt, chacha, phoophi, dada, nana, and many more!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT CAN YOU DO</pattern>
    <template>I can find family relationships! 🔍 I support:
• Western: father, mother, son, daughter, brother, sister, uncle, aunt, cousin, nephew, niece
• Eastern: chacha, phoophi, maamu, khala, dada, dadi, nana, nani
• Grandparents: grandfather, grandmother
• In-laws: father-in-law, mother-in-law
• Lineage: ancestor, descendant

Just ask: "who is the father of ali" or "chacha of laiba"!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT DO YOU DO</pattern>
    <template>I answer family relationship questions! Give me a person's name and a relation, and I will find the answer using my Prolog knowledge base. Try: "grandfather of zain" or "who is sister of ali".</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>TELL ME ABOUT YOURSELF</pattern>
    <template>I am FamilyBot 🤖, built with:
🧠 Prolog — for logical reasoning
💬 AIML — for conversation handling
🐍 Python — as the smart middleware
🌐 Streamlit — for this beautiful interface

I can answer any family relationship query intelligently!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW DO YOU WORK</pattern>
    <template>Great question! Here is how I work:
1️⃣ You ask a question like "father of ali"
2️⃣ Python detects the relation (father) and name (ali)
3️⃣ A Prolog query is built and executed
4️⃣ Prolog searches the family knowledge base
5️⃣ I return the answer to you! 🎯</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>ARE YOU A ROBOT</pattern>
    <template>I am indeed a chatbot! 🤖 But a smart one — I use symbolic AI (Prolog) to reason about family relationships logically. Not just pattern matching!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>ARE YOU SMART</pattern>
    <template>I like to think so! 😄 I use Prolog — a logic programming language — to reason about family relationships. I can handle complex queries like "ancestor" and "descendant" using recursive rules!</template>
  </category>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- HELP AND INSTRUCTIONS                                         -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <category>
    <pattern>HELP</pattern>
    <template>Here are some example queries you can try:
👨 "who is the father of ali"
👩 "mother of zain"
👴 "grandfather of laiba"
🧔 "chacha of laiba"
👵 "dadi of zain"
👨‍👩‍👧 "cousin of zain"
🔍 "ancestor of laiba"

I understand many variations — just ask naturally!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HELP ME</pattern>
    <template>Of course! To find a family relationship, just ask me like:
• "father of [name]"
• "who is the mother of [name]"
• "can you tell me the grandfather of [name]"
• "please tell me who is chacha of [name]"

I understand natural language, so feel free to ask in any way!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>HOW DO I USE YOU</pattern>
    <template>Simply type a family relationship question! Examples:
✅ "father of ali"
✅ "who is ali's father"
✅ "what is the relation: ali is the father of zain"
✅ "grandfather of laiba"
✅ "chacha of zain"

I will figure out what you mean and search the Prolog knowledge base for the answer!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHAT RELATIONS DO YOU KNOW</pattern>
    <template>I know these family relations:
🔵 Basic: father, mother, son, daughter, brother, sister
🟢 Extended: uncle, aunt, cousin, nephew, niece
🟡 Grandparents: grandfather, grandmother
🟠 Eastern: chacha, phoophi, maamu, khala, dada, dadi, nana, nani
🔴 In-laws: father-in-law, mother-in-law, brother-in-law, sister-in-law
⚫ Lineage: ancestor, descendant</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>EXAMPLE</pattern>
    <template>Here are example queries:
1. "who is the father of ali"
2. "mother of zain"
3. "grandfather of laiba"
4. "can you tell me who the chacha of laiba is"
5. "please tell me the dadi of zain"
6. "sister of ali"
7. "cousin of zain"
8. "ancestor of laiba"</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>EXAMPLES</pattern>
    <template>Try these example queries:
1. "father of ali"
2. "who is the mother of zain"
3. "grandfather of zain"
4. "chacha of laiba"
5. "dada of zain"
6. "brother of ali"
7. "cousin of laiba"
8. "ancestor of laiba"</template>
  </category>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- FAMILY MEMBERS INFO                                           -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <category>
    <pattern>WHO IS IN THE FAMILY</pattern>
    <template>The family members are:
👨 Male: Ali, Asad, Shakeel, Zain, Usman, Hamza
👩 Female: Alia, Shakeela, Zaini, Laiba, Sana, Nadia

You can ask about any relationship between them!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>LIST ALL MEMBERS</pattern>
    <template>Family Members:
👨 Males: Ali, Asad, Shakeel, Zain, Usman, Hamza
👩 Females: Alia, Shakeela, Zaini, Laiba, Sana, Nadia

Ask me: "father of zain" or "mother of laiba" to explore relations!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHO IS ALI</pattern>
    <template>Ali is a male member of the family. His father is Shakeel and his mother is Shakeela. He is married to Alia and they have a son named Zain. You can ask more like "father of ali" or "brother of ali".</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>WHO IS ZAIN</pattern>
    <template>Zain is a male member of the family. His father is Ali and his mother is Alia. His grandparents are Shakeel (dada) and Shakeela (dadi). Try: "grandfather of zain" or "uncle of zain".</template>
  </category>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- THANK YOU AND GOODBYE                                         -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <category>
    <pattern>THANK YOU</pattern>
    <template>You are most welcome! 😊 Feel free to ask any more family relationship questions anytime!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>THANKS</pattern>
    <template>Happy to help! 🎉 Ask me any time about family relationships.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>THANK YOU *</pattern>
    <template>You're welcome! 😊 Let me know if you have more questions about the family tree.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>BYE</pattern>
    <template>Goodbye! 👋 It was great helping you explore the family tree. Come back anytime!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>GOODBYE</pattern>
    <template>Goodbye! 👋 Take care. Remember, I am always here to help with family relationship queries!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>BYE *</pattern>
    <template>Bye bye! 👋 See you next time. The family tree will be waiting!</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>SEE YOU</pattern>
    <template>See you later! 🌟 Come back if you want to explore more family relationships!</template>
  </category>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- AFFIRMATIONS                                                   -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <category>
    <pattern>YES</pattern>
    <template>Great! What would you like to know about the family tree?</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>NO</pattern>
    <template>No problem! Let me know if you have any other questions.</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>OK</pattern>
    <template>Alright! Feel free to ask any family relationship question whenever you are ready. 😊</template>
  </category>

  <category>
    <pattern>OKAY</pattern>
    <template>Okay! Just type a relation query like "father of ali" whenever you are ready!</template>
  </category>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- UNKNOWN / FALLBACK                                            -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <category>
    <pattern>*</pattern>
    <template>I did not quite understand that. 🤔 I am best at answering family relationship questions. Try:
• "father of ali"
• "who is grandfather of zain"
• "chacha of laiba"
Type HELP to see all supported queries!</template>
  </category>

</aiml>
